# Sensitive data

Treat customer, payment, and credential data as regulated. Do not invent a second logging or storage path.

## Never persist or emit

- Full card numbers, CVV/CVC, magnetic-stripe data, or unmasked PANs (`Order.CardNumber`, CVV fields)
- Secrets, connection strings, API keys, or tokens in source, tests, logs, or PR text
- Raw government IDs, full account numbers, or passwords

`AllowStoringCreditCardNumber` stays off unless an explicit, reviewed requirement says otherwise. Prefer gateway tokens.

## Logs and activity

- Log entity ids, statuses, and amounts. Do not log payload dumps that may contain PII or PAN.
- `ILogger` / exception messages: strip request bodies and payment fields before write.
- Who-did-what on money, permissions, or customer-data changes goes through `ICustomerActivityService.InsertActivityAsync`. Do not put PAN or secrets in the comment.

## Tests and fixtures

- Use `Payments.TestMethod` / `TestPaymentMethod`. No live cards, no production-like PANs.
- Mask emails and names in fixtures unless the test asserts those fields.

```csharp
// BAD
_logger.Information($"Paid with {request.CreditCardNumber}");

// GOOD
await _logger.InformationAsync($"Payment captured. OrderId={order.Id}, Status={order.PaymentStatus}");
```
